cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "PHI-CTRL: Physics-Hybrid Integrity Control for Fault-Tolerant Flight"
abstract: >-
  PHI-CTRL is a physics-hybrid, fault-conditioned flight control
  architecture validated on the JSBSim F-16A 6-DOF plant under actuator
  effectiveness faults. It combines an energy-hold baseline law, an
  inverse-multiplicative hybrid compensator, MRAC adaptation, an
  MMAE-style effectiveness bank, a diagnostic observer, and an optional
  MMAE-gated PPO residual policy, validated through a three-layer
  verification ladder.
